IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc26-interpretation.l4 -- section 716 (definitions for Part XXIII), the repealed sections 717 to 717.4, and the definitions
-- of sections 729(2), 729.1(2), 732.1(1) and 734.8(1) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (lines 15171-15768 of the text).
-- Layer 1 of part ccc26. Imports the keel's core only. The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws
-- Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Every function answers a MAYBE (or a number): JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING where the text
-- does not say (list not closed, "includes", silent, points outside the text, limited by its own wording). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Helpers for this part: three-valued answers (filed under section 716, the first section of the part; not a reading of the text)`

-- HELPER: Kleene "and": JUST FALSE if either answer is JUST FALSE, else NOTHING if either is NOTHING, else JUST TRUE.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 716 all of the answers` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- HELPER
        IF b EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- HELPER
        IF a EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- HELPER
        IF b EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- HELPER
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- HELPER: Kleene "or": JUST TRUE if either answer is JUST TRUE, else NOTHING if either is NOTHING, else JUST FALSE.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 716 any of the answers` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- HELPER
        IF b EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- HELPER
        IF a EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- HELPER
        IF b EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- HELPER
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- HELPER

-- HELPER: whether one date falls within the five years that end on a later date (both ends inclusive).
GIVEN `the earlier date` IS A DATE
      `the later date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 716 the earlier date falls within the five years up to and including the later date` MEANS
    `the earlier date` AT LEAST (`add years` `the later date` (0 MINUS 5)) AND `the earlier date` AT MOST `the later date`

-- HELPER: how a period counts when it is stated in months and years (days 0): months, with years counted as twelve months.
GIVEN a IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 716 the months in the period` MEANS (a's years TIMES 12) PLUS a's months

-- HELPER: how a period counts when it is stated in days only (years 0, months 0): days, less one for "less a day".
GIVEN a IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 716 the days in the period` MEANS a's days MINUS (IF a's `less a day` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

-- HELPER: the first period is at most the second. The core gives `Length of time` no order, and a bare day count is wrong across months and leap years.
-- Measure each period as whole months plus some days ("less a day" takes one day off). From any starting date, k more months add between 28k and 31k days
-- (a month has 28 to 31 days), so the gap from the first period to the second is known to lie between a least and a most number of days.
-- The first is at most the second: JUST TRUE where the least gap is 0 or more; JUST FALSE where the most gap is below 0; otherwise NOTHING (the calendar decides).
-- Two periods in days only, or with the same months, are compared exactly.
GIVEN a IS A `Length of time`
      b IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 716 the months from the first period to the second` MEANS (`s 716 the months in the period` b) MINUS (`s 716 the months in the period` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Length of time`
      b IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 716 the least days from the first period to the second` MEANS
    (IF (`s 716 the months from the first period to the second` a b) AT LEAST 0
     THEN 28 TIMES (`s 716 the months from the first period to the second` a b)
     ELSE 31 TIMES (`s 716 the months from the first period to the second` a b))
    PLUS (`s 716 the days in the period` b) MINUS (`s 716 the days in the period` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Length of time`
      b IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 716 the most days from the first period to the second` MEANS
    (IF (`s 716 the months from the first period to the second` a b) AT LEAST 0
     THEN 31 TIMES (`s 716 the months from the first period to the second` a b)
     ELSE 28 TIMES (`s 716 the months from the first period to the second` a b))
    PLUS (`s 716 the days in the period` b) MINUS (`s 716 the days in the period` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Length of time`
      b IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 716 the first period is at most the second period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 716 the least days from the first period to the second` a b) AT LEAST 0 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`s 716 the most days from the first period to the second` a b) LESS THAN 0 THEN JUST FALSE   -- HELPER
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- HELPER

§ `Section 716 -- Definitions ("In this Part,")`

-- The headings of Part XXIII and "In this Part," are not operative (reason 1); the definitions follow, one function per defined term.

-- src:15176 | accused includes a defendant; (accusé)
@ref s 716 "accused" (src:15176)
DECLARE `s 716 who is charged` IS ONE OF
    `s 716 an accused`
    `s 716 a defendant`
    `s 716 another person, not named in the definition of accused`

@ref s 716 "accused" (src:15176)
GIVEN who IS A `s 716 who is charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 716 accused` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `s 716 an accused` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 716 a defendant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 716 another person, not named in the definition of accused` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "accused includes a defendant"

-- "alternative measures" is shown repealed in this text: carried as a string that quotes what the text shows.
-- src:15177 | alternative measures [Repealed, 2026, c. 19, s. 60]
@ref s 716 "alternative measures" (src:15177)
`s 716 alternative measures, repealed` MEANS "alternative measures [Repealed, 2026, c. 19, s. 60]"

-- src:15178 | court means
-- src:15179 | (a) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction,
-- src:15180 | (b) a court of criminal jurisdiction,
-- src:15181 | (c) a justice or provincial court judge acting as a summary conviction court under Part XXVII, or
-- src:15182 | (d) a court that hears an appeal; (tribunal)
@ref s 716 "court" (src:15178-15182)
GIVEN `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the body is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 court of criminal jurisdiction: the body is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the body is a justice or provincial court judge acting as a summary conviction court under Part XXVII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a court that hears an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 716 court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    (`s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the body is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
           OR (`s 2 court of criminal jurisdiction: the body is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
           OR `the body is a justice or provincial court judge acting as a summary conviction court under Part XXVII`
           OR `the body is a court that hears an appeal`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF    (`s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the body is one` EQUALS NOTHING)
           OR (`s 2 court of criminal jurisdiction: the body is one` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is a court of criminal jurisdiction is for s 2 and is not determined
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "court means"

-- src:15183 | fine includes a pecuniary penalty or other sum of money, but does not include restitution. (amende)
@ref s 716 "fine" (src:15183)
DECLARE `s 716 what the sum is` IS ONE OF
    `s 716 a pecuniary penalty`
    `s 716 another sum of money`
    `s 716 restitution`
    `s 716 a thing that is none of those`

@ref s 716 "fine" (src:15183)
GIVEN sum IS A `s 716 what the sum is`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 716 fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER sum
    WHEN `s 716 a pecuniary penalty` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 716 another sum of money` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 716 restitution` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include restitution"
    WHEN `s 716 a thing that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "fine includes a pecuniary penalty or other sum of money"

